  {"id":"cb3d202d-2e06-4bd7-b8f5-9a8de8f1d69f","term":"Ping","verdict":"MINOR","suggestions":[{"field":"plain_english","severity":"Low","issue":"The definition and practical_application carry two distinct senses of 'ping' — the passive decaying artifact after a hit, and the active verb of exciting a high-Q filter/reverb with an impulse ('when pinging a reverb, they feed a click into a high-Q filter'). The plain_english only teaches the passive artifact sense, so a learner meets the unexplained active sense later without grounding.","suggestion":"Add one clause to plain_english noting the second sense, e.g. 'Engineers also use \"ping\" as a verb — feeding a short click into a resonant filter or plate to make it ring on purpose.'"}]},
